  number={},
  pages={1-5},
  abstract={Airborne Maritime surveillance involves monitoring activities for safety, security and resource control using sensor technologies like Radar, Automatic Identification System (AIS), Automatic Dependent Surveillance-Broadcast (ADS-B), Search and Rescue Direction Finder (SAR-DF) and Electro Optical Payloads. This paper introduces a force multiplication effect by multi-sensor integration of AIS, ADS-B and SAR-DF sensors through a mission computer to create a unified recognizable maritime picture enhancing situational awareness and operational efficiency. It conveys a scheme for integrating sensors with mission computer and display systems, emphasizing its contribution to effective maritime surveillance. Additionally, the paper details an integration test bed that integrates these sensors with Mission Management System (MMS) and Airborne Multifunctional Tactical Console (AMTC), showcasing their role as key components for improved airborne maritime surveillance. The implemented integration scheme improves the situational awareness manifold by multi-sensor integration.},
